Title : Crack!
New-page: true

Cick, Crack, Click, Crack.

A rifle, another, the world herself tore open. 

Ratatatatatata, the machine gun opened fire.

Not water this time, not anymore.

That great crowd, once a living, breathing, mass of flesh and hope, of pretzels or hoops, it became something else. People fell, like how flour can fall from docks, bullets hitting brick, bullets hitting...Other, fleshy, things. 
  
Screams, cut short, prayers, cut short, everything, cut short, lives, hopes, dreams, passions, lovers, miseries, all, all cut short in the fire, the hellish fire.

You tried to move, your body couldn’t obey, God, there was a hot pain in your stomach, spreading outward, like blood dripping from a cut on a paper cloth. 
  
You looked down, what a stupid impulse, even you knew that, your soaked shirt, peering from your torn jacket, dark strain, blooming.
  
The crib, you thought absurdly. The wood shavings, you never finished sanding those edges, did you?

“KARL!” 

God, no, not her, anyone but her, not like this, Erika! You thought, but it was her, her voice was your own heartbeat. You knew it, you turned your head, it was painful, you saw her. 
  
She had came back, for you, for her little Karl, you fucking stupid bitch, you thought. Don’t come back for me, fucking run! You wanted to shout, her face, that faec you swore to remember ten or so minutes ago, oh God, it was horror, her blue eyes were so wide, you wanted to cry, no, the baby, the baby...
  
No, no! Not like this, please, God, not like this, how could it end like this? Your wife, she was crying, no, no, she wasn’t, she couldn’t, this wasn’t happening. You wished to awaken from this nightmare, regret seared through you. Please, God, let me take it back, you thought, let me turn back, I can’t die, you thought. 
  
You felt like a coward, did your brothers feel the same? Dying, like a coward? Ironic, you had the same killer, didn’t you? Complicity in their cases, willingness in yours, that bitter contempt

“Erika, run!” You tried to scream, those thoughts, they wore you down, it was a whisper, a wet thing, fuck, was your voice bubbling with blood? She didn’t obey, she never did, did she? She stepped forward to you, crack of a rifle, bullets sparking of cobblestones.
  
She stumbled back, a man, you didn’t see who, he grabbed her, was he a policeman?! He didn’t look like one, no, he wasn’t, that was your only relief, he grabbed her by the arms, pulling her, she tried to fight him, but she couldn’t. 
  
She was screaming, oh God, “Karl! Karl! Get up! Karl!” She was slowly quietening, but it was a blood curdling scream, she screamed not for you, for her own life. For everyone’s life

She was swallowed by the dark mass. 
